An explosion at an oil depot in Bangkok sent a large fireball and thick black smoke into the sky, journalists said Thursday, as local authorities urged people nearby to evacuate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8553b8ac-e971-11f1-8ef4-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP1207040864.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8553b8ac-e971-11f1-8ef4-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP1207040864.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72c11a30-e972-11f1-8284-6f98a01e1255</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:27:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8553b8ac-e971-11f1-8ef4-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP1207040864.jpg">© Sakchai Lalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Aid cuts to Taliban-ruled Afghanistan further curb women's access to healthcare, education and food</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/aid-cuts-to-taliban-ruled-afghanistan-further-curb-women-s-access-to-healthcare-education-and-food</link><description>
Having lived and worked in Afghanistan for seven years, photojournalist Élise Blanchard offers an intimate account of what daily life is like for Afghan women today. Joining Genie Godula on the International Day for the Elimination of Violence against Women, she explains how restrictions vary across the country, depending on where women live, their families and the local enforcement of Taliban decrees. She stresses the need to maintain access to healthcare, primary education and food, pointing to severe cuts in humanitarian assistance by the US and EU.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e4d0574-e969-11f1-9df4-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-131050-131748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e4d0574-e969-11f1-9df4-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-131050-131748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43e79814-e969-11f1-8e2d-3f120d7eed16</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:28:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Unacceptable': China, EU among major economies against new US tariffs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-unacceptable-major-economies-push-back-against-new-us-tariffs</link><description>
China, the European Union and other major trading partners on Thursday criticised new US tariffs of up to 20 percent proposed by US President Donald Trump after a probe into alleged global overcapacity, raising the prospect of fresh trade tensions with allies and rivals alike.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f00084ba-e966-11f1-9d8b-3b869f56b586</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:16:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg">© Dado Ruvic, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU leaders face showdown over Ukraine funding as divisions deepen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen</link><description>
European Union leaders on Thursday are set to tackle deep divisions as they meet in Brussels to discuss the bloc's long-term budget in Brussels, which includes a proposed €45 billion loan to keep Ukraine funded through 2027. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c93d6544-e963-11f1-80e0-0b530df5f565</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:56:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iraqi court sentences 8 French nationals to life in prison for IS group membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261126-iraqi-court-to-sentence-20-french-nationals-for-is-group-membership</link><description>
An Iraqi court sentenced eight French nationals to life in prison and two others to 15 years on Thursday for joining the Islamic State group, as Baghdad steps up prosecutions of thousands of alleged jihadists transferred from Syria.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a96c6cc4-e95e-11f1-8b02-1bf770abc0af</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:28:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60ee952-e960-11f1-829c-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19153526752150.jpg">© Khalid Mohammed, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'It’s really outrageous': Women face violence in the streets and 'what we see online is even worse'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261126-it-s-really-outrageous-women-face-violence-in-the-streets-and-what-we-see-online-is-even-worse</link><description>
On International Day for the Elimination of Violence against Women, FRANCE 24's François Picard is pleased to welcome back Choralyne Dumésnil, an attorney practising in Paris and California, to discuss misogyny, sexual violence, cyberbullying and the challenges victims face in seeking justice. "There's always that stigma when you lodge a complaint. You get questioned, you get cross-examined," notes François Picard. Despite efforts to raise awareness, Dumésnil sees little significant change in society.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dd23b16-e91b-11f1-b396-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-181554-182305-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9dd23b16-e91b-11f1-b396-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-181554-182305-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">182adc14-e95e-11f1-8ec5-57b875c9eebc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:56:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Trump, NATO chief urge Moscow to not 'expand' Ukraine war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-live-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen</link><description>
US President Donald Trump and NATO chief Mark Rutte urged Russia not to escalate its war with Ukraine, calling for swift resolution after talks in Florida on Wednesday. EU leaders are set to clash in Brussels on Thursday over a proposed €45 billion loan to fund Ukraine in 2027, with Germany pressing members to contribute and others seeking exemption. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0790aff6-e94e-11f1-9858-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26189376961541.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0790aff6-e94e-11f1-9858-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26189376961541.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e21235e-e949-11f1-968f-a7bfed69f39a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:44:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0790aff6-e94e-11f1-9858-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26189376961541.jpg">© Francisco Seco, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>US authorises SpaceX to launch up to one million satellites for orbital data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261126-us-authorizes-spacex-to-launch-up-to-one-million-satellites-for-orbital-data-centers</link><description>
The US Federal Communications Commission has approved SpaceX's plan to deploy up to one million satellites to build data centres in orbit, giving Elon Musk's company a major foothold in the industry. The authorisation runs through 2040, as tech firms race to move computing infrastructure into space despite significant technical hurdles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c24be946-bb40-11f1-b551-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T131913Z-1185617274-RC2CSNAEMW2N-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c24be946-bb40-11f1-b551-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T131913Z-1185617274-RC2CSNAEMW2N-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d5f8b8e2-e945-11f1-84ad-4378b0b17573</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:02:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c24be946-bb40-11f1-b551-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T131913Z-1185617274-RC2CSNAEMW2N-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg">© Steve Nesius, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>At least 31 killed in Cairo fire after fuel truck overturns on busy highway</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261126-at-least-31-killed-in-cairo-fire-after-fuel-truck-overturns-on-busy-highway</link><description>
At least 31 people were killed and 15 injured when a fuel truck overturned and burst into flames on a busy highway in Cairo on Wednesday, engulfing nearby vehicles, Egyptian authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac48570e-e937-11f1-b861-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329710858344.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac48570e-e937-11f1-b861-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329710858344.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5391f010-e938-11f1-b846-df9d5930b598</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:25:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac48570e-e937-11f1-b861-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329710858344.jpg">© Mohammed Salah, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Powerful US storm forces historic postponement of New York's Thanksgiving Day Parade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-powerful-us-storm-forces-historic-postponement-of-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york</link><description>
A powerful storm forecast to bring fierce winds and heavy rain to the northeastern United States has forced the unprecedented postponement of the city's 100th annual Thanksgiving Day Parade, with the event rescheduled for Saturday. Officials warned that Thursday's conditions could bring down tree limbs and power lines, while posing a safety risk to the parade's giant balloons and the crowds below.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41965f6a-e936-11f1-8632-13afe90628d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:11:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg">© Yuki Iwamura, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Duran Duran guitarist Andy Taylor dies aged 65</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261125-duran-duran-guitarist-andy-taylor-dies-aged-65</link><description>
Andy Taylor, whose guitar riffs helped shape Duran Duran's distinctive sound and propel the British band to global fame in the 1980s, has died aged 65 after a long battle with prostate cancer, the band and his family said Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/968794c0-e928-11f1-a2c5-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/063-53536468KV127-Fashion-Rocks.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/968794c0-e928-11f1-a2c5-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/063-53536468KV127-Fashion-Rocks.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27f793ec-e929-11f1-8ecb-0d5fef4a3732</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:37:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/968794c0-e928-11f1-a2c5-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/063-53536468KV127-Fashion-Rocks.jpg">© Peter Kramer, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>PSG's perfect Champions League record ends as Roma snatch 2-2 draw with late penalty</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261125-psg-s-perfect-champions-league-record-ends-as-roma-snatch-2-2-draw-with-late-penalty</link><description>
Donyell Malen's 78th-minute penalty earned Roma a 2-2 draw at Paris Saint-Germain on Wednesday, ending the defending champions' perfect record in this season's Champions League. The result also halted PSG's 12-game winning streak in all competitions, leaving Real Madrid as the only team with a 100% record after five league-phase matches.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2a6672a-e921-11f1-971b-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329749471569.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2a6672a-e921-11f1-971b-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329749471569.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43eeecdc-e922-11f1-8f87-03f1d4a69240</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:47:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2a6672a-e921-11f1-971b-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329749471569.jpg">© Teresa Suarez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Le Pen party leaks: prefect dismissed, Paris deputy prosecutor placed under investigation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-party-leaks-prefect-dismissed-paris-deputy-prosecutor-placed-under-investigation</link><description>
Two senior figures in France have been caught up in an investigation into suspected leaks to the far-right party of Marine Le Pen, the National Rally. The prefect of the Loiret, Hugues Moutouh, a former top official at the Interior Ministry, has been removed from his post after being suspected of passing on confidential information about investigations. And a deputy prosecutor in Paris, who was found at the party's headquarters during a police search, is now under administrative inquiry. FRANCE 24's Camille Knight reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1d2a0a0-d094-11f1-92d3-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298597827263.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1d2a0a0-d094-11f1-92d3-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298597827263.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">23eb5c02-e91f-11f1-b229-f3cb722aa6e0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:28:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli lawmakers advance October 7 inquiry opposed by Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-lawmakers-advance-october-7-inquiry-opposed-by-netanyahu</link><description>
Israel's new parliament on Wednesday took a first step to set up a state commission of inquiry into the security failures that led to Hamas's unprecedented October 7, 2023 attack, a move long opposed by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30dabc2c-d09d-11f1-a1eb-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T174015Z-1419027181-RC2T9OAZQPTJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-RALLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30dabc2c-d09d-11f1-a1eb-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T174015Z-1419027181-RC2T9OAZQPTJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION-RALLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">deb33278-e91d-11f1-bbce-f955831d9273</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:26:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261125-new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Dean Baker, Senior Economist at the Centre for Economic and Policy Research, says that "there has to be some mechanism for better coordinating China's involvement in the world trade system and ideally the US, the EU, Canada would have a common front, some clear ground rules that we could agree to, that China could agree to, to be mutually beneficial. It's not a step in that direction, we have President Trump lashing out really indiscriminately. It's very hard to see his approach being very productive".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fca69cc-e91c-11f1-99e8-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-223111-224208-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fca69cc-e91c-11f1-99e8-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-223111-224208-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7187f4d6-e91d-11f1-a3c9-152d2507c1bd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:13:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Dean Baker, Senior Economist at the Centre for Economic and Policy Research, says that "there has to be some mechanism for better coordinating China's involvement in the world trade system and ideally the US, the EU, Canada would have a common front, some clear ground rules that we could agree to, that China could agree to, to be mutually beneficial. It's not a step in that direction, we have President Trump lashing out really indiscriminately. It's very hard to see his approach being very productive".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fca69cc-e91c-11f1-99e8-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-223111-224208-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fca69cc-e91c-11f1-99e8-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-223111-224208-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">755e49e4-e91c-11f1-9b50-6922dcda68b9</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:11:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Cape Town court shuts down Ramaphosa's Farmgate scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cape-town-court-shuts-down-ramaphosa-s-farmgate-scandal</link><description>
In tonight's edition, South Africa's president sidesteps an impeachment bid by the opposition. Also, we hear from some of the Malagasy women fighting for an overhaul of reproductive rights in their country. And in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo,  the CRP  rebel group halts its advance after coming within dozens of kilometers of the northeastern city of Bunia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9494a8c-e917-11f1-a550-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/DN00001671-VOD-00013447-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9494a8c-e917-11f1-a550-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/DN00001671-VOD-00013447-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47ee50ca-e918-11f1-abf2-7ff6950b734e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:41:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Did GTA 6 really recreate Charlie Kirk's assassination?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261125-did-gta-6-really-recreate-charlie-kirk-s-assassination</link><description>
Just days after its release, Grand Theft Auto 6 has become a vehicle for political misinformation. Viral footage falsely claims the game features a mission recreating Charlie Kirk’s assassination, while pro-Russian accounts are sharing fake screenshots containing anti-Ukrainian messages. Meanwhile, Russia’s own Defence Ministry has exploited the game's popularity to promote military recruitment. Vedika Bahl explains how GTA 6 is being used to push real political agendas in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4913008-e90f-11f1-aa05-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/gta-6.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4913008-e90f-11f1-aa05-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/gta-6.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2c41209e-e910-11f1-8463-01391fb2df09</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:38:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Campaign rules for influencers? French regulator targets content creators</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261125-campaign-rules-for-influencers-french-regulator-targets-content-creators</link><description>
Ever since 1965 when the French first got to cast a ballot by universal suffrage for their president, they've valued campaign rules that guarantee ‘equal time’ for candidates. But what does equal time mean when you're closing in on 2027? Last week a bombshell announcement ahead of next Spring’s presidential elections: major online content creators will have to respect the same balanced air time rules as traditional TV and radio broadcasters during the campaign period. Here at France 24, we’re already testing the stopwatches and combing ove the guest list spreadsheets. Should podcasters, YouTubers and influencers be subjected to the same rules as us?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/521590aa-e903-11f1-bda6-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/Interview-en-split-screen-Macron-et-Hugo-D%C3%A9crypte.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/521590aa-e903-11f1-bda6-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/Interview-en-split-screen-Macron-et-Hugo-D%C3%A9crypte.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e0591768-e900-11f1-b948-399e8ea8d974</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:55:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU says 'strongly' rejects premise of new US tariffs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-strongly-rejects-premise-of-new-us-tariffs</link><description>
The EU said Wednesday that it rejected the premise of new tariffs on its exports proposed by the United States and expected Washington to stick by a deal struck with Brussels last year. The US unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d88720f4-e908-11f1-ab85-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-203356-203840-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d88720f4-e908-11f1-ab85-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-203356-203840-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddbab02c-e908-11f1-8992-01a3940a6265</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:48:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In boost for Netanyahu, judges question corruption trial charges</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/in-boost-for-netanyahu-judges-question-corruption-trial-charges</link><description>
Judges in the long-running corruption trial of Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu handed his defence a major boost on Wednesday in recommending the prosecution drop one of the cases in which he is accused of bribery. The recommendations, which came as Israel's longest-serving prime minister fights for his political survival, were immediately cheered by Netanyahu's right-wing allies who demanded the trial be brought to an end. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc479688-e905-11f1-9b30-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-201038-201315-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc479688-e905-11f1-9b30-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-201038-201315-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1ce860c-e905-11f1-b91f-3305ae4b2a65</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:28:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland says will create no-fly zone at Ukraine border after repeated airspace violations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-says-will-create-no-fly-zone-at-ukraine-border-after-repeated-airspace-violations</link><description>
Poland will soon create a no-fly zone near the Ukrainian border, a deputy defence minister announced on Wednesday, after several incursions into its airspace it blamed on Russia. Poland backs Ukraine as it fights off Russia's near five-year invasion and has repeatedly accused Moscow of seeking to target Kyiv's supporters with drone incursions and other methods. The no-fly zone is intended to allow Polish forces to quickly identify any Russian military aircraft and shoot them down if necessary. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/008c6c02-e905-11f1-b02d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200844-201037-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/008c6c02-e905-11f1-b02d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200844-201037-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06520944-e905-11f1-9844-d78cece7454c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:22:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US unveils proposed tariffs on major partners, including EU and China</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-unveils-proposed-tariffs-on-major-partners-including-eu-and-china</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production -- the latest move by US President Donald Trump to remake Washington's trade relationships. The duties, proposed at up to 20 percent, come over allegations the economies "are promoting production and capacity divorced from the realities of demand and market principles," a senior US official said on condition of anonymity. FRANCE 24's Camille Knight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/204bc0b6-e904-11f1-8964-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200200-200343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/204bc0b6-e904-11f1-8964-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200200-200343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25f5f7f2-e904-11f1-a905-d777088cfb1f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:15:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>The ‘French Milei’? Presidential candidate David Lisnard aims to reshape France’s right wing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261125-french-milei-presidential-candidate-david-lisnard-aims-reshape-france-right-wing</link><description>
Having secured reelection victory Wednesday as leader of France's mayors, Cannes Mayor David Lisnard turns once more to build on his recent bid for the Élysée. As his Nouvelle Énergie movement gains momentum, questions swirl over whether his campaign will reshape the French political landscape, or if his party will ultimately cosy up to the far right ahead of France’s 2027 race to the polls.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4432cb4-e8f0-11f1-9c76-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KT7H4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4432cb4-e8f0-11f1-9c76-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KT7H4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">abb4915e-e8ec-11f1-815c-19884702b0eb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:59:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4432cb4-e8f0-11f1-9c76-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D8KT7H4.jpg">© Julien de Rosa, AFP</source><dc:creator>Ella ARWYN JONES</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
